OL,3,ARaye, Rosalia and Dolly Parton
OL,4,Arecognised in Grammy nominations
OL,5,
OL,6,FBritish singer Raye leads the charge at
OL,7,Fthis year's Grammy Awards with 11
OL,8,Fnominations, while Dolly Parton has
OL,9,Fbeen recognised with two posthumous
OL,10,Fnods.
OL,12,FRaye is nominated for her latest
OL,13,FMercury-winning record This Album May
OL,14,FContain Hope and its lead single Where
OL,15,FIs My Husband!, which is up for both
OL,16,Fsong and record of the year.
OL,18,FOther nominees include Rosalia, Ella
OL,19,FLangley, Olivia Dean, Ariana Grande,
OL,20,FBruno Mars, Taylor Swift, Olivia
OL,21,FRodrigo, Miranda Lambert and Phoebe
OL,22,FBridgers.
OL,23,APub: 16-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG14/19
